# ONE-OFF PATCH SCRIPTS, WHICH MUST NEVER REACH A COMMIT.
#
# Edits to this repo are often applied by writing a throwaway `_name.py` that
# rewrites a source file and is then discarded. Five of them were committed and
# pushed on 2026-08-25 because the cleanup step was a `mv` into _to_delete/ and
# the bridge cannot unlink, so every one of those moves failed silently while
# the run reported success. Ignoring the pattern is the fix that does not
# depend on remembering.
_*.py

# scratch: files the Cowork bridge cannot delete without a permission grant
_to_delete/
